That's what I had in mind and why I added OpType as an associated type. Cast a box to a pointer, do what you need to do and cast it back. The problem is that you can't do that with the current update api because the function consumes `T` and returns an `Option<T>`. My current work around is this:
```rs
impl<T: AtomicCas + Copy> {
    pub fn fetch_update<F>(&self, set_order: Ordering, fetch_order: Ordering, f: F) -> Result<T, T>
    where
        F: FnMut(T) -> Option<T>,
    { ... }

    pub fn try_update(
        &self,
        set_order: Ordering,
        fetch_order: Ordering,
        mut f: impl FnMut(T) -> Option<T>,
    ) -> Result<T, T> { ... }

    pub fn update(
        &self,
        set_order: Ordering,
        fetch_order: Ordering,
        mut f: impl FnMut(T) -> T,
    ) -> T { ... }
}
```

