```quote
3. 似乎还会滑向这样一种局面：Cell 将内部可变性泄漏到周围区域（`&Cell` 必须假定其外部的字节也具有内部可变性，因此 `&StructContainingCell` 在某种程度上就必须假定其所有字段都具有内部可变性），
```

我意识到自己在这点上可能错了：如果我们通过从 `&StructContainingCell` 投影到某个字段来创建一个 `&Cell`，从那里越界并修改一个非 `Cell` 字段，然后再通过 `&StructContainingCell` 检查该字段，那么显然，如果一个非 `Cell` 字段的值在 `&` 引用背后发生了变化，就已经发生了 UB。也就是说，`&Cell` 是否获得对相邻内存的读写权限，这个 opsem 问题实际上并不会影响这样一种优化：在一次不透明调用的两侧读取两次非 `Cell` 字段。

```rust
struct StructContainingCell {
  a: usize,
  b: Cell<usize>,
}

fn method(s: &StructContainingCell) {
  if s.a !== 0 {
    return;
  }
  // &Cell<usize> sent to some opaque call - opsem wise it has RW rights to `s.a`
  opaque_call(&s.b);
  // SAFETY: if this fails then UB has happened - `&StructContainingCell` lives for the duration of `opaque_call` and therefore mutation of `a` would violate &-reference invariants.
  unsafe { assert_unchecked(s.a == 0) };
}
```

620038969.en:
The type of the reference is irrelevant here. The subobject provenance restriction happens at the point where the field projection happens. A reference which has permissions to access outside its type and one which doesn't have the same Rust type, they just have different provenance.

This means that specifying  whether a field projection gets subobject provenance should be done with an attribute on the field itself:

```rust
struct Foo {
    #[header]
   header: u8,

    field: u8,
    ...
}

// x has permissions to access all of Foo.
let x = &foo.header;

// y only has permissions to access the u8 field.
let y = &foo.field;
```

620038969.zh:
这里引用的类型无关紧要。子对象溯源限制发生在字段投影的地方。一个拥有访问其类型之外区域权限的引用，和一个没有这种权限的引用，它们的 Rust 类型相同，只是溯源不同。

这意味着，应该通过字段本身的属性来指定字段投影是否获得子对象溯源：

```rust
struct Foo {
    #[header]
   header: u8,

    field: u8,
    ...
}

// x has permissions to access all of Foo.
let x = &foo.header;

// y only has permissions to access the u8 field.
let y = &foo.field;
```

