619800548.en:
The discussion in https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/160202 made me wonder about `unnamed_addr` on consts and promoteds... that has a similar problem in principle, right? The following function is unsound:
```rust
fn make_slice_eq(a: &[u8], b: *const [u8]) -> &[u8] {
  // SAFETY: these point to the same memory, and that memory must be
  // initialized and immutable based on the safety invariant of `a`.
  if a.addr() == b.addr() && a.len() == b.len() { unsafe { mem::transmute(b) } }
  else { a }
}
```
We could have const A that's 0-initialized, and const B that's uninitialized. We take `&[u8]` slices to A and `*const [u8]` to B and pass them to `make_slice_eq`. We get back a pointer to static B, i.e., to uninit memory.

619800548.zh:
https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/160202 中的讨论让我开始思考 const 和 promoteds 上的 `unnamed_addr`……原则上这也存在类似的问题，对吧？下面这个函数是不健全的：
```rust
fn make_slice_eq(a: &[u8], b: *const [u8]) -> &[u8] {
  // SAFETY: these point to the same memory, and that memory must be
  // initialized and immutable based on the safety invariant of `a`.
  if a.addr() == b.addr() && a.len() == b.len() { unsafe { mem::transmute(b) } }
  else { a }
}
```
假设我们有一个零初始化的 const A，以及一个未初始化的 const B。我们分别获取指向 A 的 `&[u8]` 切片和指向 B 的 `*const [u8]`，然后将它们传给 `make_slice_eq`。这样得到的将是一个指向静态 B 的指针，也就是指向未初始化内存的指针。

619801146.en:
or maybe more like the fn example
```rust
fn with_slice_eq(a: &[u8], b: *const [u8], f: impl FnOnce(&[u8])) {
  // SAFETY: these point to the same memory, and that memory must be
  // initialized and immutable based on the safety invariant of `a`.
  if a.addr() == b.addr() && a.len() == b.len() { f(unsafe { mem::transmute(b)) } }
}
```
Now if `f` accesses the slice, after inlining it looks to LLVM as if it would directly access the uninit slice, which it may well optimize to UB based on our `noundef` annotations

619801146.zh:
或者更确切地说，可能应该像下面这个函数示例：
```rust
fn with_slice_eq(a: &[u8], b: *const [u8], f: impl FnOnce(&[u8])) {
  // SAFETY: these point to the same memory, and that memory must be
  // initialized and immutable based on the safety invariant of `a`.
  if a.addr() == b.addr() && a.len() == b.len() { f(unsafe { mem::transmute(b)) } }
}
```
现在，如果 `f` 访问这个切片，那么内联之后，在 LLVM 看来，它似乎会直接访问未初始化的切片；根据我们的 `noundef` 注解，LLVM 很可能会将其优化成未定义行为。

