615014571.en:
@_**Finley Huggins (robofinch)|1080025** [said](https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/136281-t-opsem/topic/Memory.20accesses.20that.20trigger.20signal.20handlers/near/614939545):
```quote
Or, as in the above scenario, can it not be guaranteed that a custom signal handler would run at the expected time?
```

no.
```rust
ATOMIC.store(1, SeqCst);
VOLATILE.store(2);
```
the compiler is allowed to reorder these two. if we guaranteed the signal handler to run at the volatile store, you'd be guaranteed to see the value 1 in ATOMIC, but in practice that guarantee can violated.

