623526456.en:
To better understand why this extra parameter may be needed, consider the following alternative implementation of `intensive_work`:

```rust
fn intensive_work(name: &'_ own String) -> Result<bool, &'_ own String> {
    let s = *name; // "deref-move" the referee into a local. `name` (and `*name`) are now deemed consumed/moved out of.
    let b = Box::new(s); // now put the `String` into an unrelated heap location
    // leak ownership of the *backing* heap allocation, but preseve ownership of the `String` itself.
    let own2: &'static own String = Box::leak_owned(b);
    Err(own2)
}
```

With this implementation, doing `person.name = { *rejected };` makes sense: we move out `*own2` (from the (leaked) heap), and write/init back such a value in the exhausted `person.name` place.

However, doing `person.name <- rejected;`, *i.e.*, zero-cost-"notarizing" `person.name` as initialized, would not be legal, as `person.name` is exhausted (*e.g.*, what if `intensive_work()` had even actually done `drop(s)`, and put a different string in the heap?).

That's what the `<place 'P>` invariant parameter achieves: `Box::leak_owned()`'s output would be `&'static own<'NoPlace> String`, which would be incompatible with the expected `&'_ own<'P> String` output of my `<place 'P>`-annotated signature:

```rust
fn intensive_work<place 'P>(name: &'_ own<'P> String) -> Result<bool, &'_ own<'P> String> {
    // `'NoPlace` would probably be `= 'static`, but I'm keeping this name to avoid confusion.
    let own2: &'_ own<'NoPlace> String = Box::leak_owned(Box::new(String::from("…")));
    Err(own2) // Error, `&'_ own<'NoPlace> String` does not subtype/fit `&'_ own<'P> String`
}
```

623526456.zh:
为了更好地理解为什么可能需要这个额外的参数，请考虑以下替代实现`intensive_work`:```rust
fn intensive_work(name: &'_ own String) -> Result<bool, &'_ own String> {
    let s = *name; // "deref-move" the referee into a local. `name` (and `*name`) are now deemed consumed/moved out of.
    let b = Box::new(s); // now put the `String` into an unrelated heap location
    // leak ownership of the *backing* heap allocation, but preseve ownership of the `String` itself.
    let own2: &'static own String = Box::leak_owned(b);
    Err(own2)
}
```通过这种实现，`person.name = { *rejected };`有道理：我们搬出去`*own2`（从（泄露的）堆中） ，并在耗尽的`person.name`地点。

然而，做`person.name <- rejected;`， *即* ，零成本- “公证”`person.name`作为初始化，将是不合法的，因为`person.name`疲惫不堪（ *例如* ，如果`intensive_work()`甚至实际上已经做到了`drop(s)`，并在堆中放入不同的字符串？ ）。

这就是`<place 'P>`不变参数实现：`Box::leak_owned()`的输出将是`&'static own<'NoPlace> String`，这将与预期不兼容`&'_ own<'P> String`my的输出`<place 'P>`-带注释的签名：```rust
fn intensive_work<place 'P>(name: &'_ own<'P> String) -> Result<bool, &'_ own<'P> String> {
    // `'NoPlace` would probably be `= 'static`, but I'm keeping this name to avoid confusion.
    let own2: &'_ own<'NoPlace> String = Box::leak_owned(Box::new(String::from("…")));
    Err(own2) // Error, `&'_ own<'NoPlace> String` does not subtype/fit `&'_ own<'P> String`
}
```

623731194.en:
@_**Jacob Lifshay|229517** [said](https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/131828-t-compiler/topic/Handling.20cycles.20in.20layout.20computations/near/623688739):
```quote
and then things like `transmute` size checking and `improper_ctypes` can use the layout query and not try to stuff all the complexity into the naive-layout query.
```

The issue is with situations like these:

```rust
fn f<T, U>(t: std::ops::Range<&T>) -> std::ops::Range<&U> {
  unsafe { std::mem::transmute(t) }
}
```

The transmute check runs pre-mono, so it ends up computing the layout of "`for<T> Range<&T>`", so to speak. Currently this works fine, as the layout doesn't depend on what `T` is, but with reference niches this isn't true anymore, and so `layout_of(for<T> Range<&T>)` has to return `TooGeneric`. Still, this code should compile (even if the layout depends on `T`, the size and the alignment don't), so the naive-layout query needs to be able to return an exact result here (you could say: "let's introduce a third query", but this makes the sync issues even worse).

623731194.zh:
@_* * Jacob Lifshay | 229517 * * [说] （https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/131828-t-compiler/topic/Handling.20cycles.20in.20layout.20computations/near/623688739):
```quote
and then things like `transmute` size checking and `improper_ctypes` can use the layout query and not try to stuff all the complexity into the naive-layout query.
```问题在于以下情况：```rust
fn f<T, U>(t: std::ops::Range<&T>) -> std::ops::Range<&U> {
  unsafe { std::mem::transmute(t) }
}
```变换检查在单曲前运行，因此它最终计算了“`for<T> Range<&T>`“，可以这么说。目前这个工作正常，因为布局不依赖于`T`是，但对于参考利基，这不再是真的，所以`layout_of(for<T> Range<&T>)`必须返回`TooGeneric`。尽管如此，此代码应该可以编译（即使布局取决于`T`） ，因此朴素布局查询需要能够在此处返回确切的结果（您可以说： “让我们引入第三个查询” ，但这会使同步问题更加严重）。

623765682.en:
@_**The 8472|330154** [said](https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/131828-t-compiler/topic/Handling.20cycles.20in.20layout.20computations/near/623761753):
```quote
It seems more like we want the SizeSkeleton for a pointee than a partial Layout
```

Which is sort-of what the naive layout query did in my old PR; roughly:
```rs
impl SizeSkeleton {
  pub fn compute(t: Ty) -> Option<Self> {
    // deals with "simple" potentially-generic layouts
    if let Ok(layout) = naive_layout_of(t) {
      return Self(layout.size, layout.align);
    }

    // deals with more complex layouts, but doesn't support generic references
    if let Ok(layout) = layout_of(t) {
      return Self(layout.size, layout.align);
    }

    None
  }
}
```

